cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ForgeLM in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "ForgeLM"
abstract: >-
  Config-driven LLM fine-tuning: validated YAML in, a fine-tuned model and an
  audit trail out. Covers SFT, DPO, SimPO, KTO, ORPO and GRPO, with optional
  dataset auditing, safety evaluation, evaluation gates, human approval and
  EU AI Act compliance artifacts. The same configuration runs from a terminal,
  a notebook, or a CI/CD pipeline.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ForgeLM Contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/HodeTech/ForgeLM"
url: "https://hodetech.github.io/ForgeLM/"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - llm
  - fine-tuning
  - lora
  - qlora
  - peft
  - trl
  - dpo
  - grpo
  - reproducibility
  - mlops
  - eu-ai-act
  - ai-governance
# `version` and `date-released` are intentionally omitted for now: the released
# version is single-sourced in `pyproject.toml` (read at runtime by
# `forgelm/_version.py` via `importlib.metadata`, which carries no literal of its
# own) and the site's displayed version is derived from `CHANGELOG.md` by
# `tools/update_site_version.py --check`. This file is not one of that tool's
# targets, so a version here would be an un-guarded copy that no check keeps in
# sync — exactly what `docs/standards/release.md` exists to prevent. Extending the
# tool to rewrite this file (and adding a Zenodo DOI for citable releases) is
# tracked separately.
